<title>BANGLADESH: Cargo handling ceases at Bangladesh's Mongla port.</title>
<headline>Cargo handling ceases at Bangladesh's Mongla port.</headline>
<dateline>KHULNA, Bangladesh 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>A dispute between workers and the Stevedores Association has stopped the handling of cargo at Bangladesh's southern Mongla port, port officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The workers walked out in protest on Tuesday night after the association rejected their demand for recruiting more labourers.</p>
<p>The officials said the port authorities were negotiating with the workers' union to settle the dispute which has stranded 16 ships, including one carrying foodgrains.</p>
</text>
